    "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical design for a prompt regression test. The goal is to compare the performance of an existing prompt set against a new set using a consistent model configuration. We will use a fixed suite of 12 test prompts, covering both cases where answers are expected and where the provided information is insufficient to form an answer. The comparison methodology involves running both the old and new prompt sets against the same model, using identical settings to isolate the prompt's impact. It's crucial to note that this is a hypothetical experiment, and no actual performance improvement results are available at this stage. The focus is on the methodology for setting up such a test. We aim to establish a baseline for future evaluation. The next step would be to execute these tests and analyze the outputs. Any insights on structuring such a regression test, especially concerning the handling of insufficient information cases, would be valuable.",
