    "body": "I'm exploring the design for a hypothetical prompt regression test. The objective is to rigorously evaluate changes in prompt engineering by comparing a current set of prompts against a revised set. This hypothetical framework would utilize a fixed dataset of 12 test prompts, designed to include scenarios with clear answers and others where the information provided is insufficient for a definitive response. The core of the test involves running both prompt sets on the same model, maintaining identical model settings and parameters. This approach ensures that any observed differences can be attributed to the prompt variations themselves. It's important to emphasize that this is a conceptual exercise; no actual tests have been run, and therefore, no performance improvements or regressions have been measured or observed. The current stage is purely about defining the testing methodology. Future steps would involve execution and analysis. I'm interested in feedback on this proposed test design, particularly regarding the structure for handling insufficient information cases within a regression context.",
